From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:38:15 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 59/62] dt-bindings: power: supply: add the Maxic MT5806 pen
 charger

The MT5806 is a wireless power transmitter of Maxic Technology. The
OnePlus Pad 4 uses it to charge the pen on the magnet side of the
tablet. Describe it: an I2C device with an interrupt, four control
lines (power switch, wake, scan interval, transmitter off) and the two
voltages of its supply, which comes from a boost converter owned by
the charger firmware.

Add the vendor prefix "maxic".

[adapted for the Ubuntu iceland port: carried unchanged from the Fedora
iceland queue (iceland-linux patches/0002-iceland/0091); applies to
Perpetua 7c98a10e6bb7 (the vendor-prefixes.yaml hunk at an offset).
The schema was not run through dt_binding_check on the build host:
dt-schema is not installed there.]

Exit: drop when Perpetua takes the Fedora port's pen-charger series (the Fedora port's to submit); applied untouched at the pin bump to b7d639cfb282 (2026-11-02).

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: John Stockdale <jstockdale@gmail.com>
